WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.590
You're on Mars,

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.217
it's not
particularly welcoming.

00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:11.053
So, you'll need
the essentials.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.015
♪♪

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.183
Food.

00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:17.184
Water.

00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:18.101
Air.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.102
Shelter.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:19.686
And....

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.148
Hopefully a powerful
source of energy

00:00:23.148 --> 00:00:24.650
to help survive
your new home.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:27.236
I'm Wrenn Schmidt,

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:29.154
and we're exploring the science

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.656
behind "For All Mankind."

00:00:35.661 --> 00:00:37.871
What would it take
to survive on Mars?

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.040
Like our stranded
For All Mankind crew?

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:46.797
They could stretch what
they brought with them,

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:49.883
but to generate the supplies
they need long term,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.885
they'll need a lot of power.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.889
Fortunately our crew
could harness

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.599
the limitless energy technology

00:00:57.599 --> 00:00:59.059
that helped define this season.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.689
Nuclear fusion.

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:07.150
So, why is fusion more powerful

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.528
than the atomic energy we
already create?

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:12.322
Fission with an "I."

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.408
Is nuclear power
as we know it.

00:01:14.408 --> 00:01:16.410
[ping pong sounds]

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:19.496
It splits an atom
which releases energy,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.294
[buzzer]

00:01:25.294 --> 00:01:27.504
but it also creates
radio active waste.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:30.507
[alarm]

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.510
Fusion on the other hand,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:34.761
fuses two Atoms.

00:01:38.307 --> 00:01:40.100
This releases a lot more energy.

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:42.936
And if you use an
element like Helium 3,

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.980
you'll create a lot less waste.

00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:50.527
So where could
we find Helium 3?

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:54.906
Solar winds have
been blasting

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:56.658
the moon for
billions of years.

00:01:57.284 --> 00:02:00.245
Depositing an estimated
1.1 million tons

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:02.080
of Helium 3 on the surface.

00:02:02.748 --> 00:02:04.875
We'd only 25 tons to power the

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.877
United States for
an entire year.

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:10.339
How can we get this powerful
resource from the moon?

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:13.633
Well the way they mine
Helium 3 in the show

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.510
is a blueprint for
what we can do.

00:02:16.511 --> 00:02:18.513
Using a bucket wheel excavator

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:20.891
we could collect that
Helium rich lunar reglet.

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:25.354
Heat it to  700 degrees

00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:27.230
celsius to release
the Helium 3.

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:29.149
Along side Oxygen

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.192
and Hydrogen.

00:02:30.192 --> 00:02:32.527
Two other valuable
resources in space.

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:34.613
Which we'd separate and store.

00:02:35.322 --> 00:02:37.657
Finally we'd transport
the Helium 3

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.910
to Mars to use
an infusion reactor.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.246
Giving us the
power we need to

00:02:43.246 --> 00:02:46.166
generate the essentials
for sustaining life.

00:02:48.377 --> 00:02:50.003
Nuclear fusion

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:53.173
could power the future
of life on Mars.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.342
Scientists are still trying to

00:02:55.342 --> 00:02:56.968
crack how to get
more energy outta

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.388
fusion reactions
then they put in.

00:02:59.388 --> 00:03:01.264
But the future fueled by

00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:03.392
safe abundant clean energy.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.352
Good for Mars.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:06.353
Great for Earth.

00:03:07.104 --> 00:03:08.897
Game changing
For All Mankind.

